# SEO / Content Rules

## SEO model
Every page must support:
- clear search intent
- trust
- conversion
- internal linking
- locale-aware metadata

## Metadata
Metadata must support:
- title
- description
- canonical
- hreflang alternates
- og
- twitter if used

Do not leave generic metadata placeholders on production pages.

## Page roles
Conversion pages:
- home
- alcohol
- drugs
- gambling
- family help
- rehabilitation
- contacts

Trust pages:
- about
- living conditions
- reviews
- faq

Content layer:
- blog / articles

## Avoid
- duplicate homepage wording across all pages
- generic low-value SEO filler
- aggressive claims
- medical overpromises
- page cannibalization between services and rehab/family/faq pages

## Tone
Approved tone:
- clear
- professional
- supportive
- non-judgmental

## Brand wording
Use brand naturally as:
- Rehabilitation center Renaissance

## Service page logic
Service pages are structured around:
- problem
- treatment
- recovery
- family support
- trust
- FAQ
- CTA
- related links

## FAQ logic
FAQ should be:
- data-driven
- grouped when needed
- reusable across page types

## Content generation rule
If approved copy exists, preserve it.
Do not simplify strong locked wording without reason.